Title: Bind each acceptance fail-control to its intended assertion in the normal gate
Created: 2026-09-04
Author: codex

--- log ---
2026-09-04T10:00Z codex created

--- body ---

## Context

Child of tracker `0648`. The fixture gate currently asks only whether every
assertion was red against any fixture. An unrelated failure can therefore keep
an assertion "covered" after its intended observation has broken. The fixture
gate is also outside `make check`, while the ordinary tests do not directly
exercise all advertised R15 controls.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] declare the intended assertion-to-fail-control mapping in executable form
- [ ] fail when the designated control does not produce `fail`, even if another
      fixture makes that assertion red
- [ ] assert that each control fails for its intended evidence, not merely its
      verdict token
- [ ] cover the R15 under-declaration and uninstall-residue controls in the
      normal offline gate
- [ ] keep integration-only tracer work outside the fast gate where necessary
      without dropping the R15 logic controls
- [ ] `make check` passes
